#issuecomment-4282061310","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118549","id":4282061310,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_OxH-","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-20T15:18:58Z","updated_at":"2026-04-20T15:18:58Z","body":"@brycehutchings If you can reproduce the crash semi-reliably and could validate whether #118678 fixes it, that would be super helpful. The bug report #115173 is a rare crash found in the wild on Android which we haven't managed to reproduce reliably.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4282061310/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4284196590","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118549#issuecomment-4284196590","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118549","id":4284196590,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_W6bu","user":{"login":"brycehutchings","id":5100250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDAyNTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5100250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings","html_url":"https://github.com/brycehutchings","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-20T20:51:00Z","updated_at":"2026-04-20T20:51:00Z","body":"> [@brycehutchings](https://github.com/brycehutchings) If you can reproduce the crash semi-reliably and could validate whether [#118678](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118678) fixes it, that would be super helpful. The bug report [#115173](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115173) is a rare crash found in the wild on Android which we haven't managed to reproduce reliably.\n\nI've applied #118678, but it unfortunately does not fix the issue. I even added a print inside the `while (dereference_count.get())` spin loop but never saw the code path get hit.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4284196590/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4285853789","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118549#issuecomment-4285853789","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118549","id":4285853789,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_dPBd","user":{"login":"brycehutchings","id":5100250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDAyNTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5100250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings","html_url":"https://github.com/brycehutchings","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-21T04:06:55Z","updated_at":"2026-04-21T04:07:50Z","body":"I spent more time trying to understand the problem. This is what it looks like to me:\n\nGDScript (`GDScriptLanguage`) stores all native classes and engine singletons as Variants in its globals array during init(). For ref-counted objects, this Variant holds a strong reference, keeping the object alive.\n\nDuring shutdown:\n1. GDScriptLanguage::finish() clears scripts but not the globals array.\n2. GDExtensionManager::deinitialize_extensions(SCENE) runs and frees the ObjectGDExtension metadata for every extension class registered at SCENE level.\n3. Any extension-class instance still alive now has a dangling _extension pointer.\n4. ~GDScriptLanguage finally destroys the globals array. Each Variant holding a ref-counted extension object calls RefCounted::unreference(), which dereferences the freed _extension to invoke the extension's unref callback which causes a crash.\n\nSo I think the issue is that any singleton ref-counted object registered by GDExtension will cause ~GDScriptLanguage to release the last reference which hits a code path with now-freed memory (ObjectGDExtension). Here's a screenshot of the crash while in my debugger showing _extension struct is corrupted and the crash is while accessing the Object's `_extension` field.\n\n<img width=\"1544\" height=\"769\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/913e5af8-0738-44d3-8df8-d0d3d037e38e\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4285853789/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4288289536","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118549#issuecomment-4288289536","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118549","id":4288289536,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_mhsA","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-21T11:50:42Z","updated_at":"2026-04-21T11:50:42Z","body":"Thanks for looking into it more! \n\nCan you share how you register the singleton in your code? And perhaps how you interact with it during the headless export?\n\nThank you!\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4288289536/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4291492929","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118549#issuecomment-4291492929","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118549","id":4291492929,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_yvxB","user":{"login":"brycehutchings","id":5100250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDAyNTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5100250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings","html_url":"https://github.com/brycehutchings","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-21T20:15:30Z","updated_at":"2026-04-21T20:16:21Z","body":"It just takes me doing this in my GDExtension (which has other stuff going on):\n\n```cpp\nclass CrashTest : public godot::RefCounted {\n    GDCLASS(CrashTest, godot::RefCounted)\n    static void _bind_methods() {}\n};\n\ngodot::Ref<CrashTest> g_crashTest;\n\n// register_initializer callback\nvoid initialize_module(godot::ModuleInitializationLevel level) noexcept {\n    if (level == godot::MODULE_INITIALIZATION_LEVEL_SCENE) {\n        GDREGISTER_RUNTIME_CLASS(CrashTest);\n        g_crashTest = godot::Ref<CrashTest>(memnew(CrashTest));\n        godot::Engine::get_singleton()->register_singleton(\"CrashTest\", g_crashTest.ptr());\n    }\n}\n\n// register_terminator callback\nvoid uninitialize_mrshell_module(godot::ModuleInitializationLevel level) noexcept {\n    if (level == godot::MODULE_INITIALIZATION_LEVEL_SCENE) {\n        if (g_crashTest.is_valid()) {\n            godot::Engine::get_singleton()->unregister_singleton(\"CrashTest\");\n            g_crashTest.unref();\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nNote I avoided the problem in our code by moving to raw pointer instead of Ref since there was no actual need for Ref, but it's needed for the repro.\n\nI do sometimes have to run --import 5+ times to see the crash. I also seem to have to delete the .godot cache directory. But my guess is it is all kind of random and just need the stars to align (in a bad way) to have the issue manifest as a crash.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4291492929/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4295297667","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118549#issuecomment-4295297667","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118549","id":4295297667,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAAUKgw","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-22T10:02:37Z","updated_at":"2026-04-22T10:02:37Z","body":"Thanks for the MRP! I will have a look at this later. I'm kind of leaning towards the idea that perhaps having a refcounted singleton doesn't really make much sense, semantically. But crashing is also bad!","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4295297667/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4297361206","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118549#issuecomment-4297361206","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118549","id":4297361206,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABACSHNg","user":{"login":"brycehutchings","id":5100250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDAyNTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5100250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings","html_url":"https://github.com/brycehutchings","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brycehutchings/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-22T15:02:15Z","updated_at":"2026-04-22T15:02:15Z","body":"> Thanks for the MRP! I will have a look at this later. I'm kind of leaning towards the idea that perhaps having a refcounted singleton doesn't really make much sense, semantically. But crashing is also bad!\n\nYeah ref-counted singleton didn't make sense. I'm not sure what lead this one component of ours to do it when our other singletons weren't ref-counted. Maybe developer started with a non-singleton ref counted object and changed it to a singleton but left it ref counted? But then `register_singleton` should error out if it isn't supported.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4297361206/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4303297101","html_url":"